    "highlights": "- Heavy use of stylistic sets (`.ss01`) on the primary display font (Matter) to alter letterforms for branded headings.\n- System heavily employs `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for track lists and timestamps within the UI mockups to ensure perfect vertical alignment.\n- Component labels and utility text frequently apply CSS `color-mix()` and alpha-channel transparency for text hierarchies (e.g., text-foreground/80, text-black/50) instead of entirely separate text colors.",
    "insights": [
      "The typography system creates a clear split between marketing/brand layers and functional UI: \"Matter\" handles editorial and brand messaging, while \"-apple-system\" and \"Inter\" are strictly deployed for dense application interfaces.",
      "The brand uses exceptionally light font weights (Semilight 360, Light 270) for its massive display headings (48px - 64px), creating an elegant and technical aesthetic that contrasts nicely with the heavier weights used at small scales.",
      "\"Paper Mono\", a custom monospace font, is prominently used not just for literal code blocks but also for UI elements like command palette paths and system statuses, reinforcing a developer-centric product identity."
    ]
